      "title": "About SAM3TrackToTracks",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "This custom node helps you extract information from SAM3, producing data in the SFCI's `tracks` exchange format:\n\n* Set `label` to the name of your object (e.g. \"bee\").\n* If you are tracking more than one kind of object, separate them with commas matching SAM3's object order: \"bee, flower\". \n* Turn `store_mask_rle` off if you want smaller files and only need the outline, not the interior pixels. \n* Use `min_area` and `max_area` to filter out tracked blobs that are too small or too large. These are percentages of the total image area.\n* Use `contour_holes` to allow for donut-like regions."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 116,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1376.8722743169287,
        4263.52448854016
      ],
      "size": [
        318.4511733061379,
        88
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "About EasyTracksPreview",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "In the **EasyTracksPreview** node, the `images` inlet is optional. \n\n* You can leave it unconnected for a black background. \n* Or, connect your original video to the `images` inlet to see the tracking information drawn on top. "
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
